  "about": "Who speaks each voice-clip prefix (data/sound/voice/v<prefix>_<num>.at3). The prefix is the face id of the cut-in portrait (data/menu/face_*/<prefix>_*.gim) with a leading v. Copied from Macross Ultimate Frontier (same clips, same faces) for the 39 prefixes Ace Frontier has. Names follow work/glossary/characters.json.",
  "how_identified": "As in Ultimate Frontier, whose clips these mostly are (6,546 of 6,712 byte-identical, docs/voice_subtitles.md). Face portraits, the EBOOT pilot table (0x35D908), the operator and pilot select screens, and what the clips say (self-introductions in the 000-020 launch lines). confidence: high = portrait and clip content agree; medium = one of them; low = a guess to check.",
  "numbering": "000-020 launch and greeting lines; 100-198 combat lines shared by every pilot (same situation per number); 300-371 skills, partner and result lines; 600-699 character-specific story lines used by particular missions; 900-905 era prologue narration, already shown as English text on screen (no subtitle). Operator clips (vo0_*, vos_mis) use 000-999 for stock lines and 1000+ for mission lines; the four operators read the same script, each in their own manner."
